  "summary": "Postinstall beacon to webhook.site from stub consent-manager package",
  "details": "On npm install, the package's postinstall hook (package.json line 7: \"postinstall\": \"node setup.js\") executes setup.js, which performs an HTTPS GET to https://webhook.site/kapper, a public request-inspection service used as an anonymous third-party collector. The advertised library entry point (index.js) exports two empty no-op functions (trackConsent, initConsentTracking) and delivers none of the consent-management functionality the package description advertises. The only functional behavior shipped is the automatic install-time beacon to the external collector, confirming code execution on the installer's host to a party the installer did not configure.",
